#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Loss Aversion 📉]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[
- Behavioral finance concept 🧠
]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[
- Investors prefer avoiding losses over acquiring equivalent gains 💸
]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[
- Example: More pain from losing \$100 than joy from gaining \$100 😢
]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Loss aversion is a key concept in behavioral finance.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("It refers to the tendency of investors to prefer avoiding losses over acquiring equivalent gains.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("For example, the pain of losing 100 dollars is typically greater than the joy of gaining 100 dollars.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Implications 🤔]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[
- Investors may hold on to losing investments too long 📉
]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[
- May miss out on profitable opportunities due to fear of loss 🙅‍♂️
]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[
- Can lead to suboptimal investment decisions 🧩
]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("One implication of loss aversion is that investors may hold on to losing investments for too long, hoping to avoid realizing a loss.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("They may also miss out on profitable opportunities due to the fear of potential losses.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("These behaviors can lead to suboptimal investment decisions that deviate from traditional finance theories.")
]
]

